For each model, a reliability diagram relates the classifier’s predicted probability for that model (one versus rest) to the empirical frequency with which that model generated the data. The Expected Calibration Error (ECE) quantifies the deviation from perfect calibration:\text{ECE} = \sum_{b=1}^{B} \frac{n_b}{N} \left| \text{acc}(b) - \text{conf}(b) \right|

where the confidence range [0, 1] is partitioned into B = 10 bins, n_b is the number of samples in bin b, and \text{acc}(b) and \text{conf}(b) are the mean accuracy and confidence within that bin.

